  "narrative": "The new results strongly support the already accepted central findings but leave most borderline or null extensions inconclusive. H31, H35, H37, H38, and H40 are large precise effects: TP53-loss is associated with much weaker USP7 dependency within Avana-library screens and within CDKN2A-intact screens; MSI-high is associated with much stronger WRN dependency in adenocarcinoma; KEAP1-loss is associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency in Avana screens and adenocarcinoma. These are not independent validation samples, but they are strong internal specificity checks and I accept them as closed robustness confirmations. H27 and H28 remain clinically ambiguous: KRAS mutation and EGFR amplification show small positive signed differences in adenocarcinoma, but the point estimates are near the 10% clinical scale and the intervals include both no effect and a borderline clinically meaningful effect. I defer them rather than accept them. H33 is near-null for CDKN2A loss and USP7 dependency; because the interval still includes a possible clinically meaningful positive association, I leave it unresolved but low priority. H36 tests whether TP53 loss modifies the MSI-high WRN effect. The subgroup exposed cell has only 24 observations, and the interaction estimate is small with an interval crossing zero and extending into meaningful positive values, so it is inconclusive. H39 tests whether TP53 loss modifies the KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 effect; the estimate is near zero but not precise enough to claim no interaction, so I leave it unresolved and low priority. H41 and H42 provide no evidence that STK11 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency overall or in KEAP1-loss-free cells, but the intervals are not narrow enough to assert precise absence. I close these STK11 investigations as deprioritized inconclusive rather than as definitive nulls. I request independent validation for H20, the central reversed KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 association, because it is scientifically important and has not yet had independent validation. H6 has strong internal subset consistency and can wait until H20 validation is assessed.",
  "research_notes": "Current dataset-level accepted core: H6/H21/H22/H35 MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency; H8/H24 SMARCA4-loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency and independent validation; H15/H31/H40 TP53-loss with much weaker USP7 dependency and independent validation, not explained as CDKN2A proxy; H20/H25/H26/H37/H38 KEAP1-loss with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, reversed from initial synthetic-lethal-like expectation, now validation-requested. Closed/accepted robustness checks: H31, H35, H37, H38, H40. Borderline oncogene effects: H27/H28 unresolved deferred, small and imprecise, no strong clinically meaningful adenocarcinoma effect. CDKN2A/USP7 H33 unresolved deferred, near-null but interval too wide for absence. Interactions: H36 and H39 unresolved deferred, generally near-null but imprecise; H36 subgroup has n=24. STK11/NFE2L2 H41/H42 no support and closed as deprioritized inconclusive, not definitive absence. Remaining registered follow-ups: H29 BRCA2/WRN MSI-intact, H30 NF1/KRAS KRAS-mutation-free, H32 ARID1A/SMARCA2 SMARCA4-intact, H34 ARID1A/SMARCA2 interaction, H43 WRN/TP53 MSI-intact. After H20 validation, decide whether to validate H6 or continue specificity checks. All accepted statements remain dataset-level associations, not causal claims or generalized biological claims.",
